  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA, multi-profile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc, showing that multi-profile + avgpool is a strong aggregation strategy. Image-only is very weak (0.208), suggesting the RNA modality carries most of the signal. The key untested variable within the best-known RNA pipeline is the encoder: PCA n2000 is a simple linear projection, while scvi_n200 is a learned nonlinear variational representation. Question: Does a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) improve over PCA n2000 when paired with the best-known multi-profile + avgpool aggregation? Why this is the best next experiment: It isolates a single high-impact design choice (RNA encoder) while holding the proven-best settings fixed, giving a clean comparison. If scvi_n200 helps, it opens the door to scgpt and multimodal variants with learned encoders; if it does not, it confirms PCA is sufficient and redirects budget toward the multimodal or image-encoder questions. This maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
